##

00:00:00.908 --> 00:00:04.779 line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>Vaccines are celebrated
for their part in fighting disease.</c>

00:00:04.779 --> 00:00:06.347 line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>But, a growing group of people</c>

00:00:06.347 --> 00:00:10.718 position:58% line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>seem to believe that they endanger
our health, instead of protecting it.</c>

00:00:10.718 --> 00:00:13.955 line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>The Internet is full of stories
about allergic reactions,</c>

00:00:13.955 --> 00:00:15.489 line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>the onset of disabilities,</c>

00:00:15.489 --> 00:00:18.526 line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>and even death following
vaccination appointments.</c>

00:00:18.526 --> 00:00:22.095 position:72% line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>And, it's true vaccines can have side effects.</c>

00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:26.532 line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>Let's look at how they work,
and how dangerous they really are.</c>

00:00:37.244 --> 00:00:41.048 line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>Your immune system is a
complex army of billions of cells.</c>

00:00:41.048 --> 00:00:42.149 line:0%
<c.colorFEFEFE>Soldiers,</c>

00:00:42.149 --> 00:00:43.684 line:0%
<c.colorFEFEFE>intelligence cells,</c>

00:00:43.684 --> 00:00:45.251 line:0%
<c.colorFEFEFE>and weapons factories.</c>

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:48.322 position:67% line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>Every day, you're attacked countless times,</c>

00:00:48.322 --> 00:00:51.525 line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>but your immune soldiers alone
usually deal with that,</c>

00:00:51.525 --> 00:00:53.326 line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>so you don't even notice.</c>

00:00:53.728 --> 00:00:55.963 position:61% line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>If an infection becomes serious though,</c>

00:00:55.963 --> 00:00:59.200 line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>our intelligence cells gather
intel about the attackers</c>

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:01.736 line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>and activate our weapons factories.</c>

00:01:01.736 --> 00:01:04.070 line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>You know the weapon: antibodies.</c>

00:01:04.739 --> 00:01:09.442 position:61% line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>They're like targeted missiles produced
specifically to combat the invader.</c>

00:01:09.910 --> 00:01:14.048 line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>Unfortunately, this process takes
several days to complete.</c>

00:01:14.048 --> 00:01:17.383 line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>That gives intruders
a lot of time to do damage.</c>

00:01:17.885 --> 00:01:19.787 line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>Contrary to popular wisdom,</c>

00:01:19.787 --> 00:01:22.590 position:75% line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>what doesn't kill you doesn't make you stronger.</c>

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:26.527 position:56% line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>Our bodies really don't want
to fight serious wars over and over,</c>

00:01:26.527 --> 00:01:29.497 line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>so our immune system came up
with an ingenious way</c>

00:01:29.497 --> 00:01:31.831 position:61% line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>to get stronger and stronger over time.</c>

00:01:32.333 --> 00:01:36.303 position:59% line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>If we fight an enemy that is dangerous
enough to trigger our heavy weapons,</c>

00:01:36.303 --> 00:01:39.705 line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>our immune system automatically
creates memory cells.</c>

00:01:40.141 --> 00:01:44.578 line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>Memory cells remain in our body
for years, in a deep sleep.</c>

00:01:44.578 --> 00:01:47.080 line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>They do nothing but remember.</c>

00:01:47.982 --> 00:01:50.351 position:63% line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>When an enemy attacks for a second time,</c>

00:01:50.351 --> 00:01:52.486 line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>the slumbering memory cells awaken,</c>

00:01:52.486 --> 00:01:56.457 line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>and order coordinated attacks
and the production of antibodies.</c>

00:01:56.457 --> 00:01:58.893 line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>This is so fast and effective,</c>

00:01:58.893 --> 00:02:02.997 line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>that many infections you beat once
will never make you sick again.</c>

00:02:02.997 --> 00:02:05.766 line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>You might even be immune
against them forever.</c>

00:02:05.766 --> 00:02:09.136 position:77% line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>Which is also why little kids are constantly ill;</c>

00:02:09.136 --> 00:02:11.404 position:63% line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>they don't have enough memory cells yet.</c>

00:02:12.173 --> 00:02:17.376 position:64% line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>And this beautiful natural mechanism
is what we build on when we use vaccines.</c>

00:02:18.579 --> 00:02:20.346 line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>How Vaccines Work</c>

00:02:21.549 --> 00:02:23.684 line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>As great as memory cells are,</c>

00:02:23.684 --> 00:02:28.454 position:59% line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>obtaining them through an infection
is unpleasant and sometimes dangerous.</c>

00:02:28.823 --> 00:02:32.393 position:56% line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>Vaccines are a way of tricking
our bodies into making memory cells,</c>

00:02:32.393 --> 00:02:34.595 line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>and becoming immune to a disease.</c>

00:02:34.595 --> 00:02:36.829 position:64% line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>They pretend to be a dangerous infection.</c>

00:02:37.431 --> 00:02:41.368 line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>One way of doing this is to inject
invaders that can't do harm.</c>

00:02:41.368 --> 00:02:44.937 line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>For example, by killing them,
or by ripping them into pieces.</c>

00:02:45.272 --> 00:02:49.242 position:59% line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>Our immune systems deal with
these kinds of vaccines pretty easily.</c>

00:02:49.810 --> 00:02:53.547 position:58% line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>Sometimes, it's necessary to make
our immune system work harder though,</c>

00:02:53.547 --> 00:02:56.249 line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>to produce even more memory cells.</c>

00:02:56.784 --> 00:02:59.420 line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>Live vaccines are the real deal.</c>

00:02:59.420 --> 00:03:03.424 line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>An enemy that can punch back is
a bigger challenge than a dead one.</c>

00:03:03.424 --> 00:03:06.459 line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>But this also sounds like
a sort-of horrible idea.</c>

00:03:06.794 --> 00:03:08.662 line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>What if the germs win?</c>

00:03:08.662 --> 00:03:13.299 position:63% line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>To avoid that, we breed a sort-of
weak cousin of the real germ in the lab.</c>

00:03:14.101 --> 00:03:18.838 position:63% line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>Just powerful enough to annoy the immune
system, and create enough memory cells.</c>

00:03:19.707 --> 00:03:23.811 line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>Okay, so these are the basic
principles of vaccine use.</c>

00:03:23.811 --> 00:03:26.814 position:70% line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>They provoke a natural reaction in our bodies</c>

00:03:26.814 --> 00:03:30.451 line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>that makes us become immune
against very dangerous diseases.</c>

00:03:30.451 --> 00:03:33.320 position:64% line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>Some, like the flu virus, mutate so often</c>

00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:35.789 position:59% line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>that we need a new vaccine every year,</c>

00:03:35.789 --> 00:03:39.992 line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>but most vaccines protect us
for years, or even a lifetime.</c>

00:03:40.628 --> 00:03:42.930 line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>But, there's a catch.</c>

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:46.667 line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>Like everything in life,
vaccines have another side:</c>

00:03:46.667 --> 00:03:48.269 line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>Side effects.</c>

00:03:48.269 --> 00:03:52.271 line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>What are they, and what happens
if your child develops one?</c>

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:55.074 line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>The Risks of Vaccines</c>

00:03:55.776 --> 00:04:01.148 position:77% line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>It's complicated to directly compare the side
effects of vaccines with the effects of diseases.</c>

00:04:01.148 --> 00:04:02.216 line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>For example,</c>

00:04:02.216 --> 00:04:06.053 position:61% line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>hundreds of millions of people are
vaccinated against measles in the West,</c>

00:04:06.053 --> 00:04:10.690 line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>but there were only 83,000
cases in Europe in 2018.</c>

00:04:10.991 --> 00:04:15.396 position:58% line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>So, with numbers that different,
even mild side effects can seem scary</c>

00:04:15.396 --> 00:04:19.632 position:63% line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>compared to the bad effects of a disease
that we don't see as much anymore.</c>

00:04:20.301 --> 00:04:23.671 line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>Before the measles vaccine
became available in 1963,</c>

00:04:23.671 --> 00:04:28.274 position:58% line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>virtually every single child on Earth
contracted measles at some point.</c>

00:04:28.809 --> 00:04:33.814 position:69% line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>An estimated 135 million cases in the 1950s.</c>

00:04:33.814 --> 00:04:35.681 line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>Every single year.</c>

00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:39.787 line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>But are measles really that
dangerous in the year 2019?</c>

00:04:39.787 --> 00:04:42.888 line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>With our advanced healthcare
and new technologies,</c>

00:04:43.257 --> 00:04:46.592 position:75% line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>are they worth the risk of vaccine side effects?</c>

00:04:47.461 --> 00:04:50.831 line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>Let's do a thought experiment
based on real numbers.</c>

00:04:50.831 --> 00:04:54.034 line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>Imagine a developed country
in a parallel world.</c>

00:04:54.034 --> 00:04:57.570 line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>It has good healthcare but
people stop vaccinating.</c>

00:04:58.038 --> 00:05:02.243 line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>In this scenario, let's say ten
million children caught measles.</c>

00:05:02.243 --> 00:05:03.476 line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>What happens?</c>

00:05:04.044 --> 00:05:10.283 position:77% line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>Nine million eight hundred thousand, or 98%,
will get a high fever and a very unpleasant rash.</c>

00:05:10.751 --> 00:05:15.888 position:56% line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>Up to 800,000 of them, or 8%,
will suffer from dangerous diarrhea.</c>

00:05:16.357 --> 00:05:22.762 position:78% line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>700,000, or 7%, will suffer from an ear infection,
which can lead to permanent hearing loss.</c>

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:29.703 position:73% line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>600,000 kids, or 6%, will suffer from pneumonia
-- the most dangerous effect of measles.</c>

00:05:29.703 --> 00:05:32.605 position:58% line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>It, alone, will kill 12,000 children.</c>

00:05:33.173 --> 00:05:38.044 line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>Up to 10,000 children, or 0.1%,
will get encephalitis.</c>

00:05:38.512 --> 00:05:44.285 position:66% line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>2,500 kids, or 0.025%, will contract SSPE,</c>

00:05:44.285 --> 00:05:47.354 line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>a disease where the measles
virus lingers in their brain</c>

00:05:47.354 --> 00:05:49.455 line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>and kills them a few years later.</c>

00:05:49.823 --> 00:05:50.924 line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>Taken together,</c>

00:05:50.924 --> 00:05:56.930 position:69% line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>around 2.5 million children will suffer from
somewhat serious effects from measles.</c>

00:05:56.930 --> 00:06:01.033 line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>And, about 20,000 children
will be killed by measles.</c>

00:06:01.669 --> 00:06:03.170 line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>It doesn't stop here though.</c>

00:06:03.170 --> 00:06:07.174 position:61% line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>The kids who beat measles are left with
a severely damaged immune system</c>

00:06:07.174 --> 00:06:09.709 position:61% line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>that needs a lot of time to regenerate.</c>

00:06:10.077 --> 00:06:13.045 position:70% line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>Time for other diseases to do further damage.</c>

00:06:13.614 --> 00:06:16.450 position:64% line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>Aside from that, what's almost guaranteed</c>

00:06:16.450 --> 00:06:20.052 position:56% line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>is that your kids will have a really
bad time for about two weeks.</c>

00:06:20.621 --> 00:06:23.357 line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>Okay, but what about vaccines?</c>

00:06:23.357 --> 00:06:26.293 position:67% line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>It's only fair to look at these risks, too.</c>

00:06:26.293 --> 00:06:28.595 position:63% line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>So, let's repeat our thought experiment.</c>

00:06:28.595 --> 00:06:32.900 line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>But, this time, we vaccinate ten
million children with MMR.</c>

00:06:32.900 --> 00:06:34.934 position:58% line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>What would theoretically happen here?</c>

00:06:35.636 --> 00:06:37.171 line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>After being vaccinated,</c>

00:06:37.171 --> 00:06:40.639 line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>of our 10 million kids,
around ten percent get a fever.</c>

00:06:41.008 --> 00:06:45.012 position:58% line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>500,000, or 5%, will get a mild rash.</c>

00:06:45.012 --> 00:06:48.582 line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>Up to 100, or 0.001%,</c>

00:06:48.582 --> 00:06:52.451 position:59% line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>might have a serious allergic reaction
and will have to be treated.</c>

00:06:53.053 --> 00:06:57.024 line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>Up to ten boys, or 0.0001%,</c>

00:06:57.024 --> 00:06:59.492 position:63% line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>might get inflammation of the genitalia.</c>

00:06:59.960 --> 00:07:04.765 position:63% line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>And up to ten kids in total, or 0.0001%,</c>

00:07:04.765 --> 00:07:08.067 line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>might get the most serious
side effect: encephalitis.</c>

00:07:08.736 --> 00:07:11.405 line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>So, we vaccinated ten million kids.</c>

00:07:11.405 --> 00:07:16.208 position:67% line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>In total, around one hundred and twenty had
side effects that were somewhat serious.</c>

00:07:16.710 --> 00:07:21.447 position:70% line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>Thanks to good medical treatment in developed
regions, almost all of them will be fine.</c>

00:07:22.216 --> 00:07:23.682 line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>What about autism?</c>

00:07:24.251 --> 00:07:28.689 position:58% line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>The connection of autism and vaccines
stems from one source</c>

00:07:28.689 --> 00:07:31.490 position:63% line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>that has been disproven countless times.</c>

00:07:31.892 --> 00:07:35.195 line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>We'll link to further reading
and videos in the description.</c>

00:07:35.195 --> 00:07:40.766 line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>But, in 2019, it's fair to say that
vaccines do not cause autism.</c>

00:07:41.402 --> 00:07:43.769 line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>All right, but what about deaths?</c>

00:07:44.071 --> 00:07:48.974 position:73% line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>It's really hard to say if even a single one of
our 10 million vaccinated kids would die.</c>

00:07:50.344 --> 00:07:54.081 position:58% line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>We really did look hard and
talked to a lot of different experts.</c>

00:07:54.081 --> 00:07:55.816 line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>If we ignore self-reporting,</c>

00:07:55.816 --> 00:07:59.620 line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>we could only come up with a tiny
handful of documented cases</c>

00:07:59.620 --> 00:08:05.257 position:69% line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>for all the hundreds of millions of children
who received the MMR vaccine since 1971.</c>

00:08:06.360 --> 00:08:10.998 line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>Measles are many, many thousands of
times more dangerous for your child</c>

00:08:10.998 --> 00:08:15.167 line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>than even the absolute worst
case of vaccine side effects.</c>

00:08:15.836 --> 00:08:20.474 position:66% line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>You have to search for lethal vaccine side
effects with a huge magnifying glass</c>

00:08:20.474 --> 00:08:24.111 line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>and, even then, it's very hard
to find confirmed cases.</c>

00:08:24.111 --> 00:08:28.414 line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>While, deaths from measles
are real and easy to find.</c>

00:08:29.016 --> 00:08:34.721 line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>In 2017 alone, 110,000 people
died from measles worldwide.</c>

00:08:34.721 --> 00:08:39.026 line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>Statistically, today,
300 children will die of measles.</c>

00:08:39.026 --> 00:08:41.260 line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>One since this video started.</c>

00:08:42.129 --> 00:08:44.998 position:59% line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>You can compare vaccines to seatbelts.</c>

00:08:44.998 --> 00:08:49.102 position:59% line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>Are there weird freak accidents where
someone gets killed by their seatbelt?</c>

00:08:49.102 --> 00:08:50.503 line:92%
<c.colorFEFEFE>Well, yes.</c>

00:08:50.971 --> 00:08:54.807 position:61% line:91%
<c.colorFEFEFE>But, do you personally think it's safer
